[Submission8.Objectives]
Capture the enemy guns 
[Submission8.Description]
Your orders are:
- Capture the enemy guns 
- Set up a defensive position in front of the village of Malinki 
- Place two soldiers on the gun to use it 
- Place the soldier with the highest gunner   rating into the gunner position

Note:
- Еo select shells in an armored car, tank, cannon, etc., right-click on the arrow icon to the right of the gun in the weapon panel, a list of ammunition available for this gun will open, and then select the desired type of projectile by clicking the left mouse button. The right mouse button is used to prohibit the use of the selected type of projectile. After selecting a projectile, the icons of the gun and projectile will be highlighted in yellow, which means that the unit will use only this gun and projectile. If another projectile has already been loaded in the barrel, then reloading with the selected ammunition will be carried out only after shooting the already loaded projectile.
- The gun crew can rotate and move the gun; at least two people are needed to turn or move it.
- To achieve the best fire output and accuracy when using the guns, place the soldier with the highest gunner  rating into the gunner position.

SUN TZU’S “THE ART OF WAR”
Sun Tzu said:
Anciently the skillful warriors first made themselves invincible and awaited the enemy’s moment of vulnerability.
Invincibility depends on one’s self; the enemy’s vulnerability on him.
It follows that those skilled in war can make themselves invincible but cannot cause an enemy to be certainly vulnerable.
Therefore it is said that one may know how to win, but cannot necessarily do so.
Invincibility lies in the defense; the possibility of victory in the attack.
(…)Therefore the skillful commander takes up a position in which he cannot be defeated and misses no opportunity to master his enemy.

