[Submission9.Objectives]
Destroy the enemy tanks
[Submission9.Description]

Your orders are:
- Destroy the enemy tanks using the captured guns and your tank at Waypoint 5

To do so:
- You can specify the aiming point when attacking a target- The possible options are: AIM HIGHER, AIM FREE and AIM LOWER


Note:
- Keep in mind that each type of shell is designed for a specific purpose
- High-explosive (HE) rounds are designed to destroy enemy infantry, lightly armored vehicles and open guns.
- Armor-piercing (AP) shell is solid, prone to ricochets, has no HE charge.
- Armor-piercing capped (APC) shell is solid, less prone to ricochets, has no HE charge.
- Armor-piercing high explosive (APHE) shell is prone to ricochets, has a HE charge
- Armor-piercing composite ballistic cap (APCBC) is solid, less prone to ricochets, has no HE charge.
- Subcaliber (APCR, APDS) shell has high armor penetration, but loses it faster with increasing distance. Has no chamber charge, does less damage, has less accuracy.
- High-explosive anti-tank (HEAT) shell penetrates an obstacle with a cumulative jet, armor penetration does not depend on the distance. It also has a limited high-explosive fragmentation effect.
- Smoke projectile - designed for setting smoke screens.


SUN TZU’S “THE ART OF WAR”
Sun Tzu said:
Troops thrown against the enemy as a grindstone against eggs is an example of a solid acting upon a void.

